          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em topological manifold
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            (usually required to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+topological+space"} paracompact
            %em locally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            equipped with its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
          %p
            Often one is interested in extra structure on topological manifolds, that make them for instance into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifolds"} differentiable manifolds
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+manifolds"} analytic manifolds
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifolds"} complex manifolds
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            for more on the general concept.
          %p
            Topological manifolds form a category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TopMfd"} TopMfd
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#LocallyEuclideanTopologicalSpace Locally Euclidean topological spaces
          #LocallyEuclideanSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Euclidean+topological+space"}> locally Euclidean topological space
                )
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Euclidean+topological+space"} locally Euclidean
              if every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \supset \{x\}
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              with its
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+topology"} metric topology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                        %mo ≃
                        %mphantom
                          %mi AA
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n
                    \\overset{\phantom{AA} \simeq \phantom{AA}}{\longrightarrow}
                    U_x
                    \\subset
                    X
                    \\,.
          %p
            The “local”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+properties"} topological properties
            of Euclidean space are inherited by locally Euclidean spaces:
          #LocalPropertiesOfLocallyEuclideanSpace.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Euclidean+spaces"} locally Euclidean spaces
                are
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/T1"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi T
                            %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separated
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+space"} sober
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topological+space"} locally connected
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Euclidean+space"} locally Euclidean space
              (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyEuclideanSpace"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  satisfies the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separation axiom
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+space"} sober
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topological+space"} locally connected
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+space"} locally compact
                  in the sense that every open neighbourhood of a point contains a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
                  neighbourhood.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p Regarding the first statement:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \neq y
              be two distinct points in the locally Euclidean space. We need to show that there is an open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              around
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              that does not contain
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %p
              By definition, there is a Euclidean open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ϕ
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \underoverset{\simeq}{\phi}{\to} U_x \subset X
              around
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              does not contain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x
              does contain
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≠
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^{-1}(x) \neq \phi^{-1}(y)
              are equivalently two distinct points in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{\phi^{-1}(x)} \subset \mathbb{R}^n
              not containing
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^{-1}(y)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(V_{\phi^{-1}(x)}) \subset X
              is an open neighbourhood as required.
            %p Regarding the second statement:
            %p We need to show that the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi IrrClSub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Cl(\{-\}) \;\colon\; X \to IrrClSub(X)
            %p
              that sends points to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+closure"} topological closure
              of their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+sets"} singleton sets
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              with the set of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+closed+subsets"} irreducible closed subsets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective
              (via
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "separation+axioms#T1InTermsOfClosureOfPoints"} this lemma
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \subset X
              be an open proper subset such that if there are two open subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1, U_2 \subset X
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \cap U_2 \subset P
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \subset P
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_2 \subset P
              %a{:href => "irreducible+closed+subspace#OpenSubsetVersionOfClosedIrreducible"} this prop.
              we need to show that there exists a point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo =
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P = X \setminus \{x\}
              it its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            %p
              Now since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \subset X
              is a proper subset, and since the locally Euclidean space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is covered by Euclidean neighbourhoods, there exists a Euclidean neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %munderover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \underoverset{\simeq}{\phi}{\to} U \subset X
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \cap U \subset U
              is a proper subset. In fact this still satisfies the condition that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mtext open
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1, U_2 \underset{\text{open}}{\subset} U
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \cap U_2 \subset P \cap U
              implies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \subset P \cap U
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi P
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_2 \subset P \cap U
              %a{:href => "irreducible+closed+subspace#OpenSubsetVersionOfClosedIrreducible"} that prop.
              it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ∖
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \setminus \phi^{-1}(P \cap U)
              is an irreducible closed subset of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+space"} sober topological space
              as well as
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_1
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separation+axiom"} separated
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{R}^n
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ∖
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^{-1}(P \cap U) = \mathbb{R}^n \setminus \{x\}
            %p
              In conclusion this means that the restriction of an irreducible closed subset in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to any Euclidean chart is either empty or a singleton set. This means that the irreducible closed subset must be a disjoint union of singletons that are separated by Euclidean neighbourhoods. But by irreducibiliy, this union has to consist of just one point.
            %p Regarding the third statement:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              be a point and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \supset \{x\}
              a neighbourhood. We need to find a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
              open neighbourhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cn
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cn_x \subset U_x
            %p
              By local Euclideanness, there is also a Euclidean neighboruhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %munderover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi ϕ
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \underoverset{\simeq}{\phi}{\to} V_x \subset X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \cap V_x
              is open, also
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^{-1}(U_x \cap V_x) \subset \mathbb{R}^n
              is open. This means that there exists an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{\phi^{-1}(x)}^\circ(\epsilon) \subset \phi^{-1}(U_x \cap V_x)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msubsup
                        %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(B^\circ_{\phi^{-1}(x)}(\epsilon)) \subset X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              as required.
            %p Regarding the fourth statement:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              be a point and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \supset \{x\}
              be an open neighbourhood. We need to find a compact neighbourhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_x \subset U_x
            %p
              By assumption there exists a Euclidean open neighbourhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %munderover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi ϕ
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi x
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \underoverset{\simeq}{\phi}{\to} V_x \subset X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              the intersection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_x \cap V_x
              is still open as a subspace of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_x
              and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi x
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^{-1}(U_x \cap V_x)
              is an open neighbourhood of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^{-1}(x)  \in \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              Since Euclidean spaces are locally compact, there exists a compact neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_{\phi^{-1}(x)} \subset \mathbb{R}^n
              (for instance a sufficiently small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+ball"} closed ball
              around
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heine-Borel+theorem"} Heine-Borel theorem
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+images+of+compact+spaces+are+compact"} continuous images of compact spaces are compact
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(K) \subset X
              is a compact neighbourhood.
          %p But the “global” topological properties of Euclidean space are not generally inherited by locally Euclidean spaces. This sounds obvious, but notice that also Hausdorff-ness is a “global property”:
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (locally Euclidean spaces are not necessarily
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi T
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_2
            %p
              It might superficially seem that every locally Euclidean space (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyEuclideanSpace"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} Hausdorff topological space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+space"} metric space
            %p But this is not so, Hausdorffness is a “non-local condition”.
          %p
          #NonHausdorffManifolds.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              counter-example:
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-Hausdorff+locally+Euclidean+spaces"}> non-Hausdorff locally Euclidean spaces
                )
              %br/
              An example of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+Euclidean+space"} locally Euclidean space
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyEuclideanSpace"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-Hausdorff+topological+space"} non-Hausdorff topological space
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+with+two+origins"} line with two origins
          #PathConnectedFromConnectedLocallyEuclideanSpace.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong (connected locally Euclidean spaces are path-connected)
            %p
              A locally Euclidean space which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
              is also
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path-connected+topological+space"} path-connected
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Fix any
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PConn
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PConn_x(X) \subset X
              for the subset of all those points of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              which are connected to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              by a path, hence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PConn
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ∃
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %munderover
                            %mo →
                            %mi cts
                            %mi γ
                          %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi x
                          %mo )
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %mtext and
                        %mphantom
                          %mi a
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                          %mo )
                        %mo )
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PConn_x(X)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\left\{
                    y \in X
                    \\;\vert\;
                    \\underset{[0,1] \underoverset{cts}{\gamma}{\to} X }{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    \\left(\gamma(0) = x\right)
                    \\phantom{A} \text{and} \phantom{a}
                    \\left(
                    \\gamma(1) = y
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Observe now that both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PConn
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PConn_x(X) \subset X
              as well as its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
              are
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
            %p
              To see this it is sufficient to find for every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} on
                    %msub
                      %mi PConn
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \on PConn_x(X)
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi y
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_y \supset \{y\}
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi y
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi PConn
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_y \subset PConn_x(X)
            %p
              Now by assumption every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in X
              has a Euclidean neighbourhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi y
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \overset{\simeq}{\to} U_y \subset X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi z
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \in U_y
              a path
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \gamma \colon [0,1] \to X
              connecting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \gamma(0) = y
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \gamma(1) = z
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mover
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi γ
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↦
                              %mphantom
                                %mi AAA
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %mrow
                                %mtable
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi γ
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mn 2
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo ≤
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                      %mn 2
                                  %mtr
                                    %mtd
                                      %mover
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                      %mn 2
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo −
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                      %mn 2
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mtd
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mtd
                                      %mi t
                                      %mo ≥
                                      %mn 1
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    [0,1] &amp;\overset{\tilde \gamma\cdot\gamma}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    t &amp;\overset{\phantom{AAA}}{\mapsto}&amp;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\gamma(2t) &amp;\vert&amp; t \leq 1/2
                    \\\
                    \\tilde(2t-1/2) &amp;\vert&amp; t \geq 1/2
                    }
                    \\right.
                    }
            %p
              connects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \in U_y
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi y
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi PConn
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_y \subset PConn_x(X)
            %p
              Similarly, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              is not connected to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              by a path, then also all point in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_y
              cannot be connected to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              by a path, for if they were, then the analogous concatenation of paths would give a path from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %p It follows that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi PConn
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
